# RAG framework guardrails

When working on Nirvana IQ enterprise-rag (pipelines, API, UI, deps):

## Default stack

- UI: React (Evolution Lab + Compare)
- API: FastAPI
- Vector DB: Qdrant
- Models: OpenAI (embed + chat)
- v1–v4: plain Python only — no LangChain, LangGraph, or LlamaIndex

## When frameworks are allowed

| Versions | Allowed |
|----------|---------|
| v1–v4 | Plain Python + Qdrant + OpenAI + FastAPI only |
| v5–v7 | Optional LlamaIndex for retrieval / indexes / metadata |
| v8+ | LangGraph for agentic retrieve → check → retry |
| Any | LangChain only as thin glue — never the foundation |

## Hard rules

- Do not add LangChain / LangGraph / LlamaIndex dependencies or imports to v1–v4 unless the user explicitly overrides this guardrail in the current message.
- Do not rewrite an older pipeline version just to adopt a framework.
- Keep Qdrant as the vector store; frameworks wrap it, they do not replace it.
- React must call FastAPI only; do not put framework clients in the frontend.
- Prefer scorecard deltas over pulling in frameworks early.

If the user asks to use all three frameworks on early versions, push back once with this table, then proceed only if they explicitly override.
